without a channel change returns invalid_template and writes nothing.\",\"confidence\":0.7},{\"severity\":\"MINOR\",\"area\":\"Evidence completeness\",\"file\":\"docs/launch/wp19-notification-channels-20261016.md\",\"issue\":\"The docs and form helper copy describe LINE behaviour in detail. Examples: latest template per trigger applies to all sessions, queued notifications are stopped on edit, existing bindings are skipped, and there is a five-message cap. That behaviour lives in `line-notification-materializer.ts`, which is cited as a source but not supplied. These statements cannot be verified from this packet.\",\"evidence\":\"The docs list `src/lib/line-notification-materializer.ts` under 來源. The form `<p>` blocks assert queue and binding behaviour. No materializer source or test is supplied.\",\"impact\":\"If the materializer behaves differently, the helper text could mislead. This does not affect the \\\"SMS unavailable, Email+LINE only\\\" completion claim.\",\"recommended_fix\":\"Keep the LINE behaviour claims explicitly outside the WP-19 acceptance claim, or attach materializer evidence. Optionally shorten the unconditional helper copy.\",\"required_test\":\"Not required for WP-19 acceptance. The WP-13 or materializer tests should cover the latest-template, queue-cancel and skipped-binding statements.\",\"confidence\":0.6},{\"severity\":\"MINOR\",\"area\":\"Form/server consistency\",\"file\":\"src/lib/message-template.ts\",\"issue\":\"The form disables the Email + live_started combination, but `normalizeMessageTemplateDraft` accepts it. LINE gets a trigger allowlist and Email does not. A crafted submission could save an Email template with the live_started trigger.\",\"evidence\":\"The form has `<option value=\\\"live_started\\\" disabled={channel !== \\\"line\\\"}>`. The only server trigger restriction is `LINE_WEBINAR_TEMPLATE_TRIGGERS` for LINE.\",\"impact\":\"This is unrelated to SMS. The docs correctly leave Email trigger delivery to WP-04 and WP-13 and do not claim consistency. A template that never sends could be created through a crafted request.\",\"recommended_fix\":\"Track in WP-04 or WP-13: either reject Email + live_started on the server or document it as accepted.\",\"required_test\":\"Add a normalizer test for the Email + live_started decision.\",\"confidence\":0.6},{\"severity\":\"NIT\",\"area\":\"Residual legacy handling\",\"file\":\"src/app/(app)/messages/templates/page.tsx\",\"issue\":\"Legacy SMS and unknown-channel rows still show 編輯 and 預覽內容 links, and the DB may keep isActive=true. The UI masks this, but whether any backend dispatch path ignores non-email/line channels is not shown in the packet.\",\"evidence\":\"The list masks the status badge. The select and the docs say no schema or queue changes were made.\",\"impact\":\"This is low risk, because SMS provider sending is not implemented and the docs make no SMS delivery claim.\",\"recommended_fix\":\"Optionally confirm in a later WP that the materializer and dispatcher filter on channel in (email, line).\",\"required_test\":\"Optional dispatcher test: a legacy sms template with isActive=true produces no queue rows.\",\"confidence\":0.45},{\"severity\":\"NIT\",\"area\":\"Documentation hygiene\",\"file\":\"docs/launch/provider-decisions-research-20261016.md\",\"issue\":\"The historical handoff block is now labelled as a historical snapshot, but it still contains an AI_TEAM_HANDOFF block with CURRENT_TASK_STATUS: IN_PROGRESS. A tool or reader that scans for the block could still pick it up as current.\",\"evidence\":\"The heading is \\\"研究當時的 handoff（歷史快照）\\\". The text inside still reads \\\"CURRENT_TASK_STATUS: IN_PROGRESS\\\".\",\"impact\":\"There is a minor risk of misreading the document's status. The WP-19 decision is correctly pointed to the WP-19 doc.\",\"recommended_fix\":\"Rename the status field to HISTORICAL_TASK_STATUS, or add a \\\"SUPERSEDED\\\" marker.\",\"required_test\":\"None.\",\"confidence\":0.5}]}",
